## Summary

Implemented **tutor quick actions per section** for the lesson view.

**What was built:**
- New component `SectionQuickActions.tsx` — a `Wand2` button placed in each section header (between the regen Sparkles and edit Pencil icons) that opens a portal-rendered menu with 4 intuition-first presets (*Wyjaśnij prościej*, *Dodaj analogię*, *Dodaj przykład liczbowy*, *Rozpisz symbole wzoru*) plus a *Własna instrukcja…* textarea.
- Wired into `page.tsx`: selecting an action POSTs the instruction to the US-208 `…/sections/[id]/insert` route. While generating, a loading card shows under the anchor section and the rest of the lesson stays usable. On success the spliced lesson swaps in, the new section renders inline with a novelty highlight (`--accent-soft` + accent-border ring, reusing the regenerate highlight pattern) and an **Undo** banner that calls the `insert/undo` route. On failure a dismissable error message appears at the anchor and the lesson is untouched.

**AC coverage:**
- ✅ Menu with 4 presets + custom instruction field next to the edit icon
- ✅ Calls US-208 insert route; per-anchor loading state; rest of lesson stays interactive
- ✅ Inline render with novelty highlight + Undo banner
- ✅ Readable error at the section on failure, lesson unchanged
- ✅ All styling token-based — verified in light + dark
- ✅ Browser-verified via playwright (menu, presets, custom field, loading→highlight→undo→error all pass; only console error is the intentionally-mocked 500)
- ✅ Typecheck passes; lint introduces no new errors (one pre-existing error unchanged)
- ✅ Tests pass (the 2 `generation.test.ts` TTS failures are a pre-existing full-suite parallel filesystem race — they pass in isolation and are untouched by this UI change)

Committed as `beb966c` with `US-209.passes = true`. Dev server stopped by its PID.
